          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"undset-kristin-lavransdatter-c040d12637cd30e0\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"The highlighted words occur inside Ragnfrid’s conjectural report of Kristin’s belief: “you believed that I did not love you as much.” The love proposition is therefore represented in a strongly truth-conditional mode, though embedded under negation and belief attribution rather than uttered as a simple direct avowal. It neither undertakes a relational commitment nor functions as a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The extracted string “jeg elsket dig” omits the syntactically governing “ikke.” The full occurrence attributes to Kristin the possible belief that Ragnfrid did not love her as much as Lavrans did; Ragnfrid immediately moves to refute that belief.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"reported\",\"description\":\"Ragnfrid conjecturally reports a belief she thinks Kristin may have held—that Ragnfrid did not love her as much as her father did—rather than quoting an earlier love utterance.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"After conflict with Kristin, Ragnfrid explains that she has long perceived her daughter as less attached to her and suspects Kristin mistook maternal sorrow and reserve for deficient love. Her ensuing memories of nursing Kristin and her solemn appeal to God and the Virgin explicitly correct that supposed belief: she loved Kristin no less than Lavrans did. The scene is deeply emotional, but the narration stresses that even while tears run down her cheeks, her face and voice are calm; the occurrence remains reflective, explanatory, and propositional rather than expressive/reflexive.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg tænkte, kanhænde var det for du trodde at ikke jeg elsket dig saa meget — ikke slik som far din elsker dig.”\",\"supports\":\"The highlighted love clause is embedded under negation within Ragnfrid’s conjectural attribution of a belief to Kristin, establishing reported and truth-conditional force.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Men det vet Gud og jomfru Maria, at jeg elsket dig nok ikke mindre end Lavrans gjorde.”\",\"supports\":\"Ragnfrid explicitly corrects the attributed belief by solemnly avowing that her love for Kristin was no less than Lavrans’s, confirming that the dispute concerns the truth and degree of her loving state.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Taarerne randt nedover Ragnfrids kinder, men hendes ansigt var ganske rolig og hendes stemme ogsaa.”\",\"supports\":\"Although the scene is emotionally intense, the calm face and voice provide no positive evidence that the words themselves are a reflex-like expressive discharge; this supports E=0.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Ragnfrid gives an extended retrospective account of nursing Kristin, Kristin’s early preference for Lavrans, and Ragnfrid’s own grief and fear of losing her child.\",\"supports\":\"The sustained autobiographical explanation frames the love language as a considered account of a longstanding emotional state rather than a performative undertaking or involuntary outburst.\",\"confidence\":0.97}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the occurrence’s propositional representation of maternal love, including its embedding under negation and attributed belief. P and E are not independently supported, and no residual core force requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The surrounding later avowal is used as context for interpreting the highlighted embedded occurrence, not treated as the occurrence itself.\"}"
